  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SECTION 11: PROGRAMMING & UTC BEST PRACTICES
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="programming-utc" class="reveal" aria-label="Programming and UTC">
    <h2>9. Programming &amp; UTC Best Practices</h2>
    <p>
      When building systems that log London events, utilize standard UTC offsets rather than localized runtime timezone settings to prevent scheduling overlap issues during transitions.
    </p>

    <!-- Visual 9: London Programming Workflow -->
    <figure class="article-image-container">
      <picture>
        <source type="image/svg+xml" srcset="/assets/london-programming-workflow.svg" />
        <img 
          src="/assets/london-programming-workflow.svg" 
