       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="common-mistakes" class="reveal" aria-label="Common Mistakes">
    <h2>10. Common Time Zone Mistakes to Avoid</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Writing GMT during the Summer:</strong> Writing "GMT" in June is incorrect because London is on BST (UTC+1). This can cause software logs to record events 1 hour late.</li>
      <li><strong>Assuming London changes DST with the US:</strong> London transitions on the last Sunday of March and October, while the US transitions on the second Sunday of March and first Sunday of November, creating a 2-3 week variance.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

